{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/opaque"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/Opaque","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Opaque","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is no cryptography in this enum, or anywhere in this package. That is deliberate and is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"what §23.1 requires: OPAQUE needs an oblivious PRF, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hash_to_curve"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expand_message_xmd"},{"type":"text","text":", an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"envelope construction and a three-message AKE, and eleven independent implementations of that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is eleven chances to be subtly and silently wrong. The SRP-6a this replaces was arithmetic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every language can express — which here meant a hand-written big-integer modular exponentiation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pbkdf2_sha256"},{"type":"text","text":"-only limitation on top, because Swift has no Argon2 that ships on every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"supported platform."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK6OpaqueO","title":"Opaque","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Opaque","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Opaque","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumera